<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corrientes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Corrientes is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> on the east bank of the Paraná river and the capital of Corrientes Province. Founded in 1588 by Juan Torres de Vera y Aragón, it was a river port of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> colonies and, after independence, the centre of a province often in conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corrientes.jpg" alt="Corrientes" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jara-Arroyo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puente_General_Manuel_Belgrano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
